# ttychatter

ttychatter is a terminal-first AI chat client project. The goal is a robust, user-friendly terminal chat client that can send text messages and attachments to AI without needing browser interfaces.

## Flat layout

```text
c/
docs/
ttychatter.ncurses
ttychatter.ncurses.1
ttychatter.ncurses.changelog
ttychatter.python
ttychatter.python.1
ttychatter.python.changelog
ttychatter.bash
ttychatter.bash.1
ttychatter.bash.changelog
README
LICENSE
```

## Main client

`ttychatter.ncurses` is the primary interface. It is OpenRouter-first in this release.

## Configuration

```text
~/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/config
```

Important keys:

```text
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=...
MODEL=openrouter/auto
SEND_INPUT=enter
CONTEXT_TURNS=12
SESSION_DIR=~/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/sessions
ATTACHMENT_DIR=~/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/attachments
MODEL_CACHE_FILE=~/.cache/ttychatter/openrouter/models.json
CODE_ATTACHMENT_MIN_LINES=5
```

## Default directories

```text
config:      ~/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/config
sessions:    ~/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/sessions/
attachments: ~/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/attachments/
cache:       ~/.cache/ttychatter/openrouter/models.json
```

## Model browser

The model browser supports cached model lists, explicit network refresh, search, favorites, metadata display, and model testing. It does not refresh the remote model list merely because F2 was pressed.

## Code blocks

Short code blocks remain inline. Longer code blocks are saved as attachments.
